<configs>

	<!--
		=========================================================================
		THE MAIN MENU PANEL IS NOT REGISTERED HERE - AND THAT IS THE POINT
		=========================================================================

		XUi_Menu/windows.xml defines the mainMenuHelpScreens window, but nothing in this
		modlet adds it to a window_group, so nothing ever opens it and it does not appear.
		Whoever wants the panel registers it, from their own XUi_Menu/xui.xml:

		    <append xpath="/xui/window_group[@name='mainMenu']">
		        <window name="mainMenuHelpScreens" />
		    </append>

		wrapped in <conditional><if cond="mod_loaded('sphereii_help_screens')">.

		[ WHY NOT visible="false" ON THE WINDOW ]
		Because it does not work, and it is worth writing down so nobody tries it again.
		XUiV_Window.OnOpen sets base.IsVisible = true unconditionally, every time its
		group opens:

		    public override void OnOpen()
		    {
		        base.OnOpen();
		        base.IsVisible = true;
		        ...

		XUiWindowGroup.Init does set each of its windows invisible up front, which is what
		makes the attribute look like it might survive - but the main menu group opens
		immediately, OnOpen runs, and the XML value is discarded. A window in an open
		group is a visible window. The only reliable way to keep one off the screen with
		no C# is to keep it out of the group.

		Group membership is therefore the on switch, and it is a better one than a
		visibility flag anyway: an unregistered window costs nothing at runtime, where a
		hidden one is still built, still parsed, and still has its controllers running.
	-->

</configs>
